<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Horizontal travel of the *folder* page's post-commit back exit.

     Same 96dp / 450 ms contract as the shared page exit
     (DefaultCrossActivityBackAnimation retargets the closing rect to
     currentClosingRect.left + cross_activity_back_entering_start_offset, which is
     96dp). Only the shape differs: the shared resource uses fast_out_slow_in,
     whose slow start is correct for a page that is fading on top of a parent that
     is itself moving in. On the folder branch the parent does not move at all, so
     a slow start leaves the foreground hovering for the first ~100 ms and then
     dissolving before it has covered a quarter of the travel.

     Measured travel fractions (same evaluation path as the alpha curve):
         progress   fast_out_slow_in   this curve
         0.02       0.001             0.010
         0.10       0.026             0.114
         0.20       0.134             0.363
         0.26       0.261             0.535
         0.35       0.500             0.780

     So at the instant the paired alpha curve reaches 0 (35%) the page has covered
     78% of the 96dp instead of 50%. The start is still slow (1dp in the first
     9 ms) so the release frame does not kick, the middle carries the visible
     departure, and the long decelerating tail keeps the page from stopping dead
     at 450 ms.

     PathInterpolator contract: starts at (0,0), ends at (1,1), x strictly
     increasing (0.12 -> 0.20 -> 0.35 -> 0.52 -> 0.74 -> 1). -->
<pathInterpolator xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:pathData="M0,0 C0.12,0.04 0.2,0.4 0.35,0.78 C0.52,0.93 0.74,0.99 1,1" />
